---
pre-compare: sort
---
from_file env("TENZIR_INPUT") {
  read_json
}
// The stored-shape records exactly as the live lane reads them back:
// the tetragon-direct-attest probe's output as strict JSON — what the
// per-class ocsf catch-all columns hold, minus the schema-unification
// null paddings (att[0].prev_event / att[1].fingerprint), which the
// ClickHouse JSON-column write drops anyway — the tetragon-verify-
// clean discipline, on the DIRECT leg's chain. The probe's arrival
// order was adversarial: a same-second tie pair (exec/exit) arriving
// in reverse uid order, two out-of-order arrivals riding the window
// tolerance, and a late record arriving 36s behind the max observed
// clock yet stamped in its correct (time, uid) chain position. Two
// 60s windows: W1 = exec (restart head) -> exit -> kprobe -> late,
// W2 = file (restart head) -> net — the window heads carry no
// prev_event exactly like the live leg's first record after a node
// restart (the node context is not fixture-testable; the LIVE
// cross-window seam rides the tetragon-chains context and is the
// lap-2a-2 server-side item). THIS is the false-flag proof the lap
// exists for: the verify walk re-sorts the merged stream on the same
// (time, metadata.uid) pair the windowed stamp sorted on, recomputes
// every fingerprint, and checks chain adjacency — a stamping order
// that deviated from the walk's re-sort anywhere would flag
// chain_link_mismatch here. Expected: the summary line alone, zero
// findings.
fork {
  summarize records_checked = count()
  to_stdout { write_json }
}
homelab::record_integrity::verify product="homelab-detection",
  title="Detection record chain break",
  uid_prefix="detection",
  scope_word="chain",
  windowed=true,
  link="stream"
